// A silent FUSION LOSS, not a value divergence — `check` reports AGREE
// on this program in both the broken and fixed states, because the
// node-walk is the fallback and it is correct. It is here as a
// de-fusion pin: `fusecheck` is the gate that would have caught it.
//
// `emit_qop_deliver` (fusion/emit/flow.rs) emits the error-delivery
// DynCall for a handler-ful `?` — one covered by an enclosing `catch`.
// Commit 9d042cbc (2026-08-07, "fused DynCall: deliver non-fired args
// as TagValue::stale") grew `graphix_dyncall` from four parameters to
// five by adding `stale_mask`, and updated `emit/call.rs`,
// `emit_helpers.rs` and `kernel.rs` — but not `flow.rs`, the only
// other call site. `git show --stat 9d042cbc` shows the three files.
//
// Cranelift's verifier caught it, which is the good news and also why
// it hid for a month: it rejects the ENTIRE function, so the symptom
// is that the region node-walks, visible only under --fusion-stats:
//
//   define_function (shared body): Compilation error: Verifier errors:
//   - inst25 (v30, v31 = call fn11(v27, v25, v28, v29)):
//     mismatched argument count for `...`: got 4, expected 5
//
// Fixed by passing the explicit `stale0` (0 — the single error arg was
// already gated on `deliverable`, so it delivers FIRED). Hardened by
// `BodyCx::call_helper`, which looks the helper up and debug-asserts
// the argument count against its registered wire signature, so an
// arity mismatch panics a test instead of quietly costing fusion.
// Pinned on the value side by the `qop_handler_deliver` run! fixture
// (stdlib/graphix-tests/src/lang/errors.rs), which asserts
// FuseExpect::Jit and therefore fails outright in the broken state.
{
  let caught = i64:0;
  catch(e) caught <- e ~ i64:1;
  let a = [i64:10, i64:20];
  a[i64:0]? + i64:100
}
